angus@milton.u.washington.edu writes:
>asweatma@crc.ac.uk (A.K. Sweatman) writes:
>> Of these Stormbringer seems to be the best, but is currently -2
>> because it got corroded twice in the course of killing a rust monster.
>
>There is a good way to keep this from happening.  (Spoilers ahead)

> 
>Confuse yourself, perhaps with a potion.  While you are confused, read a 
>scroll of enchant weapon.  The weapon you are wielding, instead of becoming 
>enchanted in the usual sense, will be made rust-proof.  No effects that 
>might corrode it will work thereafter.

If you don't have the right scroll or means of confusion, then weild that 
unicorn horn that you're carrying when you meet that rust monster.  Unicorn 
horns do damage comparable to long swords.  (Very good.)  And they don't rust.

>> Is there any easy way of getting it back to +0 or better?
>
>None except using a scroll of enchant weapon.

Zapping the artifact with a wand of cancellation will return its bonus to 0.
It *will* remain an artifact.  Don't waste scrolls of enchant weapon if you
don't have to...

